# Xcode
# Xcode exports are DIRECTORIES and the deploy/build logs are FILES, so these two rules ignore both without
# needing a negation: build/cg-check.csv is a tracked file at the top level and matches neither. (The earlier
# `build/*` + `!build/cg-check.csv` worked too; plain `build/` never can -- git cannot re-include anything
# inside an excluded directory -- and `build/*/` alone leaves the generated build/ios.log trackable.)
build/*/
build/*.log
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
*.moved-aside
*.pbxuser
!default.pbxuser
*.mode1v3
!default.mode1v3
*.mode2v3
!default.mode2v3
*.perspectivev3
!default.perspectivev3

# SwiftPM
.build/
.swiftpm/
Package.resolved

# macOS
.DS_Store

# .NET (Core/Sim/FlightTests)
bin/
obj/
bin~/
obj~/
*.user

# Unity (unity/ project)
unity/Library/
# ...and the same path WITHOUT the trailing slash, because unity/Library is now a SYMLINK (2026-10-21) to
# ~/Library/Application Support/FlyingGame/unity-Library, and git sees a symlink as a file, which a
# directory-only rule does not match.
unity/Library
unity/Temp/
unity/Logs/
unity/UserSettings/
unity/obj/
# The Android (Quest) build's native scratch directory.
unity/.utmp/
# StreamingAssets is GENERATED by ConfigSync from configs/ and docs/CREDITS.md for everything listed below --
# the repo keeps ONE copy of each. Committing a generated mirror as well is the trap that let great-lakes-like
# ship with no runtime config (2026-10-30): the mirror was gitignored-but-tracked, so a new file reached the
# player only if somebody ran `git add -f`. Do not commit anything matched here, and never `git add -f` it.
# commerce.json is NOT generated -- it has no repo source and stays committed.
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/challenges/
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/challenges.meta
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/atmosphere/
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/atmosphere.meta
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/glide-table.json
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/glide-table.json.meta
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/vr-cardboard.json
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/vr-cardboard.json.meta
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/progression.json
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/progression.json.meta
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/credits.md
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/credits.md.meta
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/rigs/
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/rigs.meta
# The aircraft JSON mirrors are GENERATED and NOT versioned. Ty 2026-11-10, asked to settle the open
# decision recorded here: "Untrack them". ConfigSync writes them from configs/ on every build, so a tracked
# copy is a second source of truth that drifts, and it is exactly the trap described above -- 71 of them were
# tracked-but-ignored, which is how great-lakes-like shipped with no runtime config on 2026-10-30. It also
# cost real time on 2026-11-10: locally regenerated mirrors blocked two lane merges outright.
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/aircraft/
# aircraft.meta is the folder's OWN meta and commerce.json is written beside the mirrors, so neither was
# matched by the "aircraft/" line above. A repo-wide `git add '*.meta'` swept both into a commit on
# 2026-11-10 and blocked the very next lane merge -- the third merge this trap has cost in one day.
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/aircraft.meta
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/commerce.json
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/commerce.json.meta
*.csproj.meta
unity/*.csproj
unity/*.sln

# Secrets
*.env
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# Local automation — must NEVER land in the public repo.
# claude-run.sh executes with skipped permissions; if the repo could alter it
# or its prompt file, a repo write would become code execution on the Mac.
scripts/claude-run.sh
scripts/NEXT-PROMPT.md

# Cockpit view renders and other review artefacts written by the editor checks (generated; regenerate with
# Unity -executeMethod FlyingGame.EditorTools.CockpitEyeCheck.Run, without -nographics).
logs/

# Unity performance-test run info (generated)
unity/Assets/Resources/PerformanceTest*
unity/Assets/Resources.meta
unity/Assets/Resources/
__pycache__/

# Raw downloaded art before it is processed into unity/Assets (172 MB of zips and source trees as of
# 2026-10-20). The tracked record of a model's licence is unity/Assets/_Project/Resources/Models/<id>/LICENSE.txt;
# the copy under assets-incoming/models/<id>/ is a local note beside the download it came from.
assets-incoming/

# Agent worktrees: full checkouts of this repo (329 MB), never part of it.
.claude/worktrees/

# Tracked-vs-generated for the aircraft mirrors is SETTLED (Ty 2026-11-10): generated, not tracked, which is
# what the two StreamingAssetsTests assert. build/cg-check.csv is tracked and stays so.
